    "notes": [
      {
        "version": "0.4.12",
        "releaseChannel": "STABLE",
        "title": "SDKWork Cloud Router 0.4.12",
        "summary": "Restores a green Verify Application on main: the security scan reads its advisory allowlist again, the router-service test target compiles, and the clippy gate is clean.",
        "content": "Every push since 0.4.11 failed Verify Application, so the repository had no green baseline to release from. Three independent defects were behind it. First, the security-scan job invoked cargo audit without --file: cargo-audit reads its configuration from $CARGO_HOME/audit.toml or ./audit.toml and never from .cargo/, so the seven advisories this repository documents as unfixable here were reported on every run and the job exited 5. Second, commit 38e990d7 removed the vendor_code and modalities fields from the upstream-account-group row but left the struct literals naming them in sql_pricing_catalog_contract.rs, so the router-service test target did not compile; because cargo stops at the first crate that will not build, that failure is what surfaced the clippy backlog behind it. Third, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings reported 78 errors across five crates. The mechanical half is fixed: unused imports, redundant closures, collapsible ifs, derivable Default impls, field_reassign_with_default, unnecessary to_owned, a named tuple type, and two test harnesses holding a MutexGuard across an await. Two families are waived crate-wide with the reasoning in the source, result_large_err on axum Response returns and too_many_arguments on route assembly and relay dependency injection. Separately, one stale assertion expected a workspace pool default of 10 while DatabaseConfig::DEFAULT_MAX_CONNECTIONS is 16, and its poisoned ENV_LOCK took ten more tests down with it; the assertion now reads the constant and the lock recovers from poisoning. The dead PostgresPricingCatalogLoader::api_key_secret_storage field is removed; the real encode/decode path lives in PostgresGatewayApiKeyCommandStore and was already wired. Release notes cover only this version; earlier records stay archived under docs/release/.",
        "highlights": [
          "Verify Application is green on main for the first time since 0.4.11",
          "cargo audit reads .cargo/audit.toml, so the seven documented advisories stop failing the security scan",
          "The clippy gate is clean: 78 errors cleared across five crates, with the two waived families justified in source",
          "The database_config suite is 33 of 33: one stale pool-default assertion no longer cascades through a poisoned lock",
          "Dead API-key secret storage wiring removed from the pricing catalog loader",
          "Install-time configuration stays contract-driven for ports, PostgreSQL/SQLite, and Redis"
        ],
        "packageIds": [
          "web-universal-cloud-browser-zip",
          "web-universal-standalone-browser-zip",
          "windows-x64-standalone-desktop-zip",
          "macos-universal-standalone-desktop-dmg",
          "linux-x64-standalone-desktop-appimage"
        ],
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-18T00:00:00Z",
        "current": true,
        "forceUpdate": false,
        "minSupportedVersion": "0.4.11",
        "metadata": {}
      }
    ]
